{
  "original_id": "newwin-00001-p13",
  "archive_id": "BW2-N01-P13",
  "title": "Quadratic positivity for finite-field q-hit residues",
  "batch_label": "新WIN-1批次",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every integer n>=1, every board B subset [n] x [n], and every d in {0,...,n}, define m_i, M_i and H_d exactly as in source.md and problem.md over every prime-power field. If H_d(B,x+1) is represented modulo x^3 on all x=q-1 by its unique integer polynomial c_0+c_1*x+c_2*x^2, then c_2>=0. This full-scope theorem is proved by a balanced-restriction convolution identity expressing the quadratic hit polynomial as the classical hit family convolved with coefficientwise nonnegative kernels supported on square boards of sizes 2,3,4. No global polynomiality or positivity of higher coefficients is asserted.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
